:2281,"exampleId":381,"difficulty":1}}],"completedStr":"Completed @ 1:51 AM","exampleAnswers":[{"id":377,"number":1,"title":"Integrating the Exponential Function","answers":[{"id":62313776,"created":"2026-10-16T01:49:59.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":14072,"number":1,"createdStr":"Fri, Oct 16th @ 1:49 AM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:14","question":{"id":71914,"format":"MC","difficulty":1,"exampleId":377,"text":"<p>$\\displaystyle \\int -5e^x \\, \\textrm{d}x=$</p>\n","choice1":"$-5e^x +C$","choice2":"$-\\dfrac 1 5e^x +C$","choice3":"$5e^{5x} +C$","choice4":"$e^{-5x} +C$","choice5":"$e^{x} +C$","freeAnswerChoice":" ","explanation":"<p>Factoring out the constant $-5$ and calculating the resulting integral, we get</p>\n<p>\\[\n\\eqalign{\n\\displaystyle \\int -5e^x \\, \\textrm{d}x&= -5\\displaystyle \\int e^x \\, \\textrm{d}x\\\\\n&= -5e^x +C.\n\n\n\n\n}\n\\]</p>\n","topic":{"id":312,"name":"Integrating Exponential Functions"},"example":{"id":377,"title":"Integrating the Exponential Function"},"group":{"id":51962,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[{"id":null,"number":null,"answers":[]}],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14252829,"answer":{"id":62313776,"cread":"2026-10-16T01:49:59.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":14072},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyEasy","difficultySymbol":"E","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62313786,"created":"2026-10-16T01:50:17.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":13362,"number":2,"createdStr":"Fri, Oct 16th @ 1:50 AM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:13","question":{"id":113858,"format":"MC","difficulty":3,"exampleId":377,"text":"<p>$\\displaystyle \\int \\dfrac{\\pi}{2} e^x \\, \\textrm{d}x=$</p>\n","choice1":"$\\dfrac{\\pi}{2} e^x +C$","choice2":"$\\dfrac{\\pi}{2e^{x}} + C$","choice3":"$\\pi e^{2x}  + C$","choice4":"$2e^{\\pi x} + C$","choice5":"$\\dfrac{2}{\\pi e^{x}} + C$","freeAnswerChoice":" ","explanation":"<p>Factoring out the constant $\\dfrac{\\pi}{2}$ and calculating the resulting integral, we get</p>\n<p>\\[\n\\eqalign{\n\\displaystyle \\int \\dfrac{\\pi}{2} e^x \\, \\textrm{d}x&= \\dfrac{\\pi}{2}\\displaystyle \\int e^x \\, \\textrm{d}x\\\\[5pt]\n&= \\dfrac{\\pi}{2} e^x +C.\n\n\n\n\n}\n\\]</p>\n","topic":{"id":312,"name":"Integrating Exponential Functions"},"example":{"id":377,"title":"Integrating the Exponential Function"},"group":{"id":97427,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14252829,"answer":{"id":62313786,"cread":"2026-10-16T01:50:17.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":13362},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyHard","difficultySymbol":"H","rendered":true,"testMode":false}}]},{"id":380,"number":2,"title":"Integrating an Exponential Function With a General Base","answers":[{"id":62313796,"created":"2026-10-16T01:50:42.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":13245,"number":3,"createdStr":"Fri, Oct 16th @ 1:50 AM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:13","question":{"id":71910,"format":"MC","difficulty":3,"exampleId":380,"text":"<p>Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int \\left(\\dfrac 1 3\\right)^x \\, \\textrm d x.$</p>\n","choice1":"$- \\dfrac{\\left(\\dfrac 1 3\\right)^x}{\\ln 3} + C$","choice2":" $\\dfrac{\\left(\\dfrac 1 3\\right)^x}{3\\ln 3} + C$","choice3":" $3\\left(\\dfrac 1 3\\right)^x + C$","choice4":"$\\ln 3\\left(\\dfrac 1 3\\right)^x + C$","choice5":"$-3\\ln 3\\left(\\dfrac 1 3\\right)^x + C$","freeAnswerChoice":" ","explanation":"<p>To compute the integral of a general exponential function, we just need to divide by the natural logarithm of the base of the exponential function:</p>\n<p>\\[\n\\eqalign{\n\\int \\left(\\dfrac 1 3\\right)^x  \\, \\textrm d x   &= \\dfrac{\\left(\\dfrac 1 3\\right)^x}{\\ln\\left(\\dfrac 1 3\\right)} + C\n}\n\\]</p>\n<p>Using the laws of logarithms, we have that</p>\n<p>\\begin{align*}\n\\ln\\left(\\dfrac 1 3 \\right) \n&= \\ln 1 - \\ln 3\\\\[5pt]\n&= 0 - \\ln 3\\\\[5pt]\n&=-\\ln3.\n\\end{align*}</p>\n<p>So, we can simplify our final answer as follows:</p>\n<p>\\begin{align*}\n\\dfrac{\\left(\\dfrac 1 3\\right)^x}{\\ln\\left(\\dfrac 1 3\\right)} + C = - \\dfrac{\\left(\\dfrac 1 3\\right)^x}{\\ln 3} + C\n\n\\end{align*}</p>\n","topic":{"id":312,"name":"Integrating Exponential Functions"},"example":{"id":380,"title":"Integrating an Exponential Function With a General Base"},"group":{"id":97441,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14252829,"answer":{"id":62313796,"cread":"2026-10-16T01:50:42.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":13245},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyHard","difficultySymbol":"H","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62313811,"created":"2026-10-16T01:50:59.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":13672,"number":4,"createdStr":"Fri, Oct 16th @ 1:50 AM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:14","question":{"id":113893,"format":"MC","difficulty":3,"exampleId":380,"text":"<p>Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int \\left(\\dfrac 1 8\\right)^x \\, \\textrm d x.$</p>\n","choice1":"$- \\dfrac{\\left(\\dfrac 1 8\\right)^x}{\\ln 8} + C$","choice2":" $ \\dfrac{8^x}{\\ln 8} + C$","choice3":" $\\dfrac{\\ln x}{\\ln 8} + C$","choice4":" $-\\dfrac{\\ln x}{8^x }+ C$","choice5":" $\\left(\\dfrac{1}{8}\\right)^x\\ln 8 + C$","freeAnswerChoice":" ","explanation":"<p>To compute the integral of a general exponential function, we just need to divide by the natural logarithm of the base of the exponential function:</p>\n<p>\\[\n\\eqalign{\n\\int \\left(\\dfrac 1 8\\right)^x  \\, \\textrm d x   &= \\dfrac{\\left(\\dfrac 1 8\\right)^x}{\\ln\\left(\\dfrac 1 8\\right)} + C\n}\n\\]</p>\n<p>Using the laws of logarithms, we have that</p>\n<p>\\begin{align*}\n\\ln\\left(\\dfrac 1 8 \\right) \n&= \\ln 1 - \\ln 8\\\\[5pt]\n&= 0 - \\ln 8\\\\[5pt]\n&=-\\ln 8.\n\\end{align*}</p>\n<p>So, we can simplify our final answer as follows:</p>\n<p>\\begin{align*}\n\\dfrac{\\left(\\dfrac 1 8\\right)^x}{\\ln\\left(\\dfrac 1 8\\right)} + C = - \\dfrac{\\left(\\dfrac 1 8\\right)^x}{\\ln 8} + C\n\n\\end{align*}</p>\n","topic":{"id":312,"name":"Integrating Exponential Functions"},"example":{"id":380,"title":"Integrating an Exponential Function With a General Base"},"group":{"id":97441,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14252829,"answer":{"id":62313811,"cread":"2026-10-16T01:50:59.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":13672},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyHard","difficultySymbol":"H","rendered":true,"testMode":false}}]},{"id":381,"number":3,"title":"Integrating a Sum of Exponential Functions","answers":[{"id":62313830,"created":"2026-10-16T01:51:20.000Z","choices":null,"correct":0,"selectedChoice":2,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":13167,"number":5,"createdStr":"Fri, Oct 16th @ 1:51 AM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:13","question":{"id":2279,"format":"MC","difficulty":1,"exampleId":381,"text":"<p>$\\displaystyle \\int (4^x - e^x)\\, \\textrm{d}x = $</p>\n","choice1":"$\\dfrac{4^x}{\\ln4} - e^x +C$","choice2":"$\\dfrac{2^x}{\\ln x} - 4e^x +C$","choice3":"$-\\dfrac{4^x}{\\ln4} - e^{2x} +C$","choice4":"$\\dfrac{x}{\\ln4} -e^x +C$","choice5":"$\\dfrac{4^{2x}}{\\ln4} - 2e^x +C$","freeAnswerChoice":"","explanation":"<p>Here, we combine the sum rule and our exponential rules to get</p>\n<p>\\begin{eqnarray}\n    \\eqalign{\n     \t  \\int (4^x-e^x)  \\, \\textrm{d}x  &=   \\int 4^x \\, \\textrm{d}x - \\int e^x \\, \\textrm{d}x\\\\\n&= \\dfrac{4^x}{\\ln4} - e^x +C. \t\t\t\t\n \t\t\t\t\t\n\n \n      \n        \n    }\n\\end{eqnarray}</p>\n","topic":{"id":312,"name":"Integrating Exponential Functions"},"example":{"id":381,"title":"Integrating a Sum of Exponential Functions"},"group":{"id":52093,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14252829,"answer":{"id":62313830,"cread":"2026-10-16T01:51:20.000Z","choices":null,"correct":0,"selectedChoice":2,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":13167},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyEasy","difficultySymbol":"E","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62313841,"created":"2026-10-16T01:51:38.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":14672,"number":6,"createdStr":"Fri, Oct 16th @ 1:51 AM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:15","question":{"id":51102,"format":"MC","difficulty":2,"exampleId":381,"text":"<p>$\\displaystyle \\int \\left(2e^x+4^x-2x\\right) \\,  \\textrm{d}x=$</p>\n","choice1":"$2e^x+ \\dfrac{4^x}{\\ln4} - x^2 +C$","choice2":"$e^{2x}+ \\dfrac{4^x}{\\ln4} - x^2 +C$","choice3":"$e^{2x}+ \\dfrac{x^4}{\\ln4} - x^2 +C$","choice4":"$e^{2x}+ \\dfrac{x^4}{\\ln4} - 2x^2 +C$","choice5":"$2e^x+ 4^x\\ln4 - \\dfrac{x^2}{2} +C$","freeAnswerChoice":"","explanation":"<p>Here, we combine the sum rule and our exponential rules to get</p>\n<p>\\[\n\\eqalign{\n\\displaystyle \\int \\left(2e^x+4^x-2x\\right) \\, \\textrm{d}x&= 2\\displaystyle \\int e^x \\, \\textrm{d}x + \\displaystyle \\int 4^x \\, \\textrm{d}x - 2\\displaystyle \\int x \\, \\textrm{d}x\\\\\n&= 2e^x+ \\dfrac{4^x}{\\ln4} - x^2 +C.\n\n\n\n\n}\n\\]</p>\n","topic":{"id":312,"name":"Integrating Exponential Functions"},"example":{"id":381,"title":"Integrating a Sum of Exponential Functions"},"group":{"id":52092,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14252829,"answer":{"id":62313841,"cread":"2026-10-16T01:51:38.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":14672},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyModerate","difficultySymbol":"M","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62313855,"created":"2026-10-16T01:51:55.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":11536,"number":7,"createdStr":"Fri, Oct 16th @ 1:51 AM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:12","question":{"id":2281,"format":"MC","difficulty":1,"exampleId":381,"text":"<p>$\\displaystyle \\int (9^x + 3e^x) \\, \\textrm{d}x = $</p>\n","choice1":"$\\dfrac{9^x}{\\ln9}+3e^x +C$","choice2":"$\\dfrac{\\ln9}{9^x}+e^x +C$","choice3":"$\\dfrac{x}{\\ln9}-3e^x +C$","choice4":"$\\dfrac{9}{\\ln x}+e^{3x} +C$","choice5":"$\\dfrac{x^9}{\\ln9}-3e^x +C$","freeAnswerChoice":"","explanation":"<p>Here, we combine the sum rule and our exponential rules to get</p>\n<p>\\begin{eqnarray}\n    \\eqalign{\n     \t  \\int (9^x+3e^x ) \\, \\textrm{d}x  &=    \\int 9^x \\, \\textrm{d}x + 3 \\int e^x \\, \\textrm{d}x\\\\\n&= \\dfrac{9^x}{\\ln9}+3e^x +C.\n \t\t\t\t\t\n\n \n      \n        \n    }\n\\end{eqnarray}</p>\n","topic":{"id":312,"name":"Integrating Exponential Functions"},"example":{"id":381,"title":"Integrating a Sum of Exponential Functions"},"group":{"id":52093,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14252829,"answer":{"id":62313855,"cread":"2026-10-16T01:51:55.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":11536},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyEasy","difficultySymbol":"E","rendered":true,"testMode":false}}]}],"localGraph":{"topicId":312,"topics":[{"id":312,"name":"Integrating Exponential Functions","prerequisites":[1361],"frontier":0,"halfLife":0.3162412267350435,"repetition":1,"stability":0.09539109072773354},{"id":1361,"name":"Integrating the Reciprocal Function","prerequisites":[],"frontier":0,"halfLife":0.25683370593530147,"repetition":1,"stability":0.08485470226982396},{"id":2793,"name":"Necessary and Sufficient Conditions","prerequisites":[312]},{"id":3575,"name":"Applying the Fundamental Theorem of Calculus to Exponential and Trigonometric Functions","prerequisites":[312]}]}}}